# ai-docs-kit guidance for {{ project_name }}

This directory is the managed entry point for documentation work in this repository.
Read it first, then load only the route or skill needed for the scoped task.

## Read in this order

1. [Policy](policy.md): evidence rules for material claims and review outcomes.
2. [Project context](project.md): audience, terminology, evidence locations, local rules.
3. [Documentation home](../{{ docs_dir }}/README.md): routing index for readers.
4. [Skill catalog](skills/README.md): names, triggers, and paths. Load one skill body
   only when its trigger matches the task.

## Managed paths and ownership

| Path | Ownership |
| --- | --- |
| `.copier-answers.ai-docs-kit.yml` | Copier installation state; do not edit manually |
| `.ai-docs/README.md`, `policy.md`, `skills/`, `assets/`, `examples/`, tool configs | Managed; local edits merge through Copier |
| `.ai-docs/project.md` | Seeded once; you own it afterwards |
| `{{ docs_dir }}/` seed pages | Seeded once; you own them afterwards |

Copier may report conflicts when a managed file changed both locally and upstream.
Resolve them and rerun checks; a zero exit code alone is not proof of a clean update.

## Deterministic checks

Prerequisites, installed by you or your CI environment: `pre-commit`, Node.js 24 with
`markdownlint-cli2` 0.24.1 available to pre-commit, and a Lychee 0.24.2 binary on
`PATH`. ai-docs-kit does not install these tools.

```sh
pre-commit run --config .ai-docs/pre-commit-config.yaml --all-files
```

The command checks all Markdown under `.ai-docs/` and `{{ docs_dir }}/` on every run,
including new files:

- markdownlint-cli2 in check mode with `.ai-docs/markdownlint-cli2.jsonc`; native
  defaults apply except `MD013` (line length), which is disabled.
- Lychee in offline mode with `.ai-docs/lychee.toml`: relative files, images, and
  local heading fragments are checked; remote URLs are not requested.

It does not verify factual support, Diátaxis fit, clarity, or completeness. Those
require the review workflow in `.ai-docs/skills/docs-review/SKILL.md`.

Existing root Markdown or link configuration is not modified. `--config` selects a
base configuration; a closer consumer-native configuration can still influence files.
See [policy.md](policy.md) and your local additions in [project.md](project.md).

## Agent activation

The portable baseline is manual: read this file, then
[skills/README.md](skills/README.md), then one selected `SKILL.md`. Host-specific
automatic skill discovery is not assumed. An optional, inert routing snippet for an
existing agent instruction file is in
[examples/AGENTS.snippet.md](examples/AGENTS.snippet.md); it is never applied
automatically.

## Documentation root

The install-time answer `docs_dir` is `{{ docs_dir }}`. It names a subtree and is
unchanged by v0.1 updates. Moving it later is not supported; create a new installation
instead. Existing documents keep their paths until an explicitly reviewed
reorganization.
